<section class=\"wash section\"><div class=\"wrap\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">The scope / What we consider</span><h2>See the whole.<br>Resolve the details.</h2><div class=\"scope-list\"><article><h3>Layout &amp; everyday use</h3><p>Map how you move through the home, where belongings gather, and which rooms need privacy or connection. Compare options before adding area.</p></article><article><h3>Light &amp; comfort</h3><p>Consider orientation, shading, ventilation opportunities, and the depth of the plan. Coordinate specialist input where performance needs closer investigation.</p></article><article><h3>Character &amp; materials</h3><p>Identify elements worth retaining and assess how old and new can meet. Develop finishes and joinery with maintenance and repair in mind.</p></article><article><h3>Buildability &amp; sequence</h3><p>Review structural changes, service routes, site access, and possible phases with the relevant consultants and builder. Make the work understandable before it begins.</p></article></div><p class=\"fine-print\">A project proposal would define the exact appointment. Surveys, engineering, statutory fees, and construction costs are separate items to discuss.</p></div></section>
<section class=\"wrap section\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">The process</span><h2>One clear decision at a time.</h2><ol class=\"process-list\"><li><span class=\"number\">01</span><h3>Understand the existing</h3><p>Gather your brief, available drawings, and a condition overview. Identify the measured survey and specialist investigations needed to make informed decisions.</p></li><li><span class=\"number\">02</span><h3>Test the possibilities</h3><p>Explore a small number of layout options, including what could be achieved within the current footprint. Discuss priorities and seek cost input early.</p></li><li><span class=\"number\">03</span><h3>Develop the design</h3><p>Resolve the chosen arrangement, material direction, and key details. Coordinate consultant input and identify the relevant approval route for the site.</p></li><li><span class=\"number\">04</span><h3>Prepare for building</h3><p>Produce the agreed drawings and specifications for pricing and construction. Confirm responsibilities, information needs, and the scope of any site-stage support.</p></li></ol></section>
<section class=\"section wash\"><div class=\"wrap example-strip\">{photo('hero')}<div><span class=\"eyebrow\">An example / Fictional concept</span><h2>Courtyard House</h2><p>A narrow house becomes easier to live in by moving circulation toward a small courtyard. The front rooms remain intact, while the shared kitchen and dining space gain a direct relationship with the garden.</p><p>The lesson is simple: a change in the plan can matter more than a change in size.</p>{link('work_preview.html#courtyard-house','Read the project study')}</div></div></section>
<section class=\"wrap section faq-layout\"><div><span class=\"eyebrow\">Renovation questions</span><h2>A little clarity<br>before you start.</h2></div><div>{faq([('Can we live at home during the work?','Sometimes, but it depends on access, services, dust, noise, and the extent of structural work. Discuss this with the design team and builder early. A phased plan may help, while some projects need a temporary move.'),('Will we need planning permission?','That depends on the location, property, and proposed changes. The relevant local requirements would need to be checked for your actual project. This fictional sample cannot determine an approval route.'),('What if our budget is still uncertain?','Start with a comfortable investment range and a list of priorities. Early options can then be tested with appropriate cost advice. Keep professional fees, approvals, contingency, and temporary accommodation in the overall picture.'),('Can you guarantee a completion date?','No date can be established from an initial idea alone. Surveys, approvals, design decisions, contractor availability, and the condition of the existing building all affect the schedule. A realistic program would be developed as those unknowns become clearer.')])}</div></section>'''
